---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Nav from "../components/Nav.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";

const lastUpdated = "May 5, 2026";
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Service — Bible Seek"
  description="The terms that govern your use of the Bible Seek iOS app."
  path="/terms"
>
  <Nav />
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-16 md:py-24">
    <p class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-widest uppercase text-accent">
      Terms
    </p>
    <h1
      class="mt-3 font-serif text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold text-ink leading-tight"
    >
      Terms of Service
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-ink-muted">Last updated {lastUpdated}</p>

    <div
      class="prose prose-neutral mt-10 max-w-none text-ink-soft leading-relaxed
             [&_h2]:font-serif [&_h2]:text-2xl [&_h2]:text-ink [&_h2]:mt-12 [&_h2]:mb-4 [&_h2]:font-semibold
             [&_h3]:font-serif [&_h3]:text-lg [&_h3]:text-ink [&_h3]:mt-8 [&_h3]:mb-2 [&_h3]:font-semibold
             [&_p]:my-4 [&_a]:text-accent [&_a]:underline
             [&_ol]:my-4 [&_ol]:pl-6 [&_ol]:list-decimal
             [&_ul]:my-4 [&_ul]:pl-6 [&_ul]:list-disc [&_li]:my-1"
    >
      <p>
        These Terms of Service ("Terms") govern your access to and use of
        the Bible Seek mobile application and any related services
        (collectively, the "Services") provided by Bible Seek ("we," "us,"
        or "our"). By downloading, installing, or using the Services, you
        agree to be bound by these Terms. If you do not agree, do not use
        the Services.
      </p>
      <p>
        Please also review our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>, which
        describes how we handle information in connection with the Services
        and is incorporated into these Terms by reference.
      </p>

      <h2>1. The Services</h2>
      <p>
        <em
          >In Short: Bible Seek is a free, offline-first iOS application
          for reading and studying scripture.</em
        >
      </p>
      <p>
        Bible Seek is a Bible reader that runs entirely on your device.
        Features include verse highlighting, study notes, custom reading
        plans, memory-verse practice, and original-language word studies.
        We may add, change, or remove features at any time without prior
        notice.
      </p>

      <h2>2. License to use the Services</h2>
      <p>
        <em
          >In Short: We grant you a personal, non-transferable license to
          use the app on devices you own or control.</em
        >
      </p>
      <p>
        Subject to your compliance with these Terms, we grant you a
        limited, personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable
        license to download and use the Services on Apple-branded devices
        you own or control, solely for your personal, non-commercial use.
        This license does not allow you to use the Services on any device
        you do not own or control, and you may not distribute or make the
        Services available over a network where they could be used by
        multiple devices at the same time.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Apple App Store terms</h2>
      <p>
        <em
          >In Short: Apple's standard app license also applies, and Apple
          is not responsible for the Services.</em
        >
      </p>
      <p>
        These Terms are between you and us. Apple is not a party to these
        Terms and is not responsible for the Services or their content. To
        the extent there is any conflict between these Terms and Apple's
        Licensed Application End User License Agreement, Apple's terms
        govern only with respect to the matters they address. You
        acknowledge that:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Apple has no obligation to furnish any maintenance and support
          services with respect to the Services.
        </li>
        <li>
          In the event of any failure of the Services to conform to any
          applicable warranty, you may notify Apple, and Apple will refund
          the purchase price (if any) for the Services to you.
        </li>
        <li>
          Apple is not responsible for addressing any claims by you or any
          third party relating to the Services or your use of them.
        </li>
        <li>
          Apple and Apple's subsidiaries are third-party beneficiaries of
          these Terms and, upon your acceptance of these Terms, will have
          the right (and will be deemed to have accepted the right) to
          enforce these Terms against you.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>
        <em
          >In Short: Use the Services for their intended purpose; don't
          interfere with, copy, or attack them.</em
        >
      </p>
      <p>You agree not to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Reverse-engineer, decompile, disassemble, or otherwise attempt to
          discover the source code of the Services, except to the extent
          such restrictions are prohibited by applicable law.
        </li>
        <li>
          Modify, adapt, translate, or create derivative works based on the
          Services.
        </li>
        <li>
          Remove, obscure, or alter any proprietary notices (including
          copyright notices) on or in the Services.
        </li>
        <li>
          Use the Services to violate any applicable law, regulation, or
          third-party right.
        </li>
        <li>
          Interfere with, disrupt, or place an unreasonable load on the
          Services or any related infrastructure.
        </li>
        <li>
          Use any automated means (such as bots or scrapers) to access the
          Services in a manner that sends more requests than a human could
          reasonably produce.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Your content</h2>
      <p>
        <em
          >In Short: Notes, highlights, and other content you create stay
          on your device. We don't claim ownership of them.</em
        >
      </p>
      <p>
        Anything you create within the Services — highlights, notes,
        bookmarks, reading position, custom reading plans, memory verses,
        and tags — is yours. As described in our <a href="/privacy"
          >Privacy Policy</a
        >, this content is stored locally on your device using Apple's
        standard on-device storage and is not uploaded to any server we
        operate.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        <em>In Short: We own the app, its design, and its branding.</em>
      </p>
      <p>
        The Services, including their software, design, text, graphics,
        and the Bible Seek name and logo, are owned by us or our licensors
        and are protected by copyright, trademark, and other intellectual
        property laws. Except for the limited license granted in Section
        2, no rights are transferred to you under these Terms.
      </p>
      <p>
        Scripture text, lexicon entries, cross-references, and topical
        indexes shipped with the Services are used under the licenses of
        their respective rights holders. Where required, attribution
        appears within the Services.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Updates and discontinuation</h2>
      <p>
        <em
          >In Short: We may update or discontinue the Services at any
          time.</em
        >
      </p>
      <p>
        We may release updates to the Services that fix bugs, add features,
        or change behavior. We may also discontinue the Services or any
        portion of them at any time, with or without notice. We are not
        liable to you or any third party for any modification, suspension,
        or discontinuation of the Services.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Termination</h2>
      <p>
        <em
          >In Short: You can stop using the Services at any time by
          deleting the app. We can revoke your license if you violate
          these Terms.</em
        >
      </p>
      <p>
        These Terms remain in effect while you use the Services. You may
        terminate them at any time by uninstalling the app. We may suspend
        or terminate your right to use the Services at any time, without
        notice, if we believe you have violated these Terms or applicable
        law. Sections that by their nature should survive termination —
        including disclaimers, limitations of liability, indemnification,
        and governing-law provisions — will survive.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Disclaimer of warranties</h2>
      <p>
        <em>
          In Short: The Services are provided "as is," with no warranties.</em
        >
      </p>
      <p>
        To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, the Services
        are provided "as is" and "as available," without warranties of any
        kind, whether express or implied, including but not limited to
        warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose,
        non-infringement, accuracy, or uninterrupted operation. We do not
        warrant that the Services will be error-free, secure, or always
        available, or that defects will be corrected.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        <em
          >In Short: To the extent the law allows, our liability for
          anything related to the Services is limited.</em
        >
      </p>
      <p>
        To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, in no event
        will we be liable for any indirect, incidental, special,
        consequential, exemplary, or punitive damages, or for any loss of
        profits, revenue, data, or goodwill, arising out of or in
        connection with these Terms or your use of the Services, even if
        we have been advised of the possibility of such damages. Our total
        cumulative liability arising out of or relating to these Terms or
        the Services will not exceed the greater of (a) the amount you
        paid us for the Services in the twelve (12) months preceding the
        claim or (b) twenty United States dollars ($20).
      </p>
      <p>
        Some jurisdictions do not allow the exclusion or limitation of
        certain damages, so the above limitations may not apply to you in
        full.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Indemnification</h2>
      <p>
        You agree to defend, indemnify, and hold us harmless from and
        against any claims, liabilities, damages, losses, and expenses
        (including reasonable attorneys' fees) arising out of or in any
        way connected with your access to or use of the Services or your
        violation of these Terms.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Governing law</h2>
      <p>
        These Terms are governed by the laws of the State in which we
        reside, without regard to its conflict-of-laws principles. Any
        dispute arising out of or relating to these Terms or the Services
        will be resolved in the state or federal courts located in that
        State, and you consent to the personal jurisdiction of those
        courts. Nothing in this section limits any rights you may have
        under the consumer protection laws of your place of residence.
      </p>

      <h2>13. Changes to these Terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these Terms from time to time. The updated version
        will be indicated by an updated "Last updated" date at the top of
        this page. If we make material changes, we may notify you by
        prominently posting a notice within the Services or on our
        website. Your continued use of the Services after changes take
        effect constitutes your acceptance of the updated Terms.
      </p>

      <h2>14. Contact us</h2>
      <p>
        If you have any questions about these Terms, please email us at
        <a href="mailto:bibleseek@icloud.com">bibleseek@icloud.com</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
